Somebody just tried to sign in using <%= @provider %>, with an account whose
email address is this one.

We did not let them in, and we did not connect anything. This account has never
been connected to <%= @provider %>, and we do not link accounts just because two
email addresses happen to match — that would mean anybody able to persuade
<%= @provider %> to vouch for your address could reach your account here.

If that was you, and you would like to use <%= @provider %> to sign in from now
on, sign in the normal way first and then connect it deliberately:

<%= @url %>

If it was not you, there is nothing to do. Nobody got in and nothing changed.
